From 5f5d3588bd9e5bed5acf4931e1fa98bc540800bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:51:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(coreelec): Kodi's pause after a mode switch; no previews
 or updater

After an auto frame rate mode switch, playback now waits as Kodi's "Delay
after change of refresh rate" makes it: only when the mode really changed,
timed from the switch, for TIZENTUBE_SWITCH_DELAY_MS (Kodi's delay, from the
add-on) and never shorter than the 1 s HDMI mute, so nothing plays unseen.
Players hold their pipeline paused (a mode switch tells them through a hold
listener) and play on when the hold ends.

TizenTube itself still loads from its CDN, so its upgrades keep coming. The
page script sets the options CoreTube replaces at each start, before
TizenTube reads them: previews, the updater and TizenTube's own auto frame
rate pause are off. YouTube's preview flag is locked off, since TizenTube's
menu sets it again when an option changes. "Check for updates" never reaches
GitHub; a toast says Kodi handles updates. A pause TizenTube makes just
before SetFrameRate (its option set again in its menu) is undone at once.

Previews can no longer be turned on, so the TIZENTUBE_VIDEO_PREVIEWS switch
the shell passed to the page is gone.
